1
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:03,990
It summons magicite beasts.

2
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:06,600
Ripple!

3
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:09,000
I'm sorry!

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,230
I can't keep this up anymore!

5
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:45,060
<u>Reborn</u>

6
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:45,060
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

7
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:45,060
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

8
00:01:58,130 --> 00:02:03,050
Episode 9          A New Artifact

9
00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:01,220
My desk!

10
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:02,780
It's huge!

11
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:04,190
Be careful, Rani!

12
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:10,370
It's probably as strong as Seilyn and Rahl 
were when they became magicite beasts!

13
00:02:10,370 --> 00:02:12,900
Your words and your face 
are telling two different stories!

14
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,140
Oh, whoops.

15
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:22,830
<i>It's a different color,</i>

16
00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:26,120
<i>but I feel the same flow of power 
as I did when I saw those heat rays.</i>

17
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:27,700
<i>Which means...</i>

18
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:31,460
It's probably going to fire 
heat rays everywhere!

19
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,410
S-Stop it, please!

20
00:02:33,810 --> 00:02:35,260
Of course.

21
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,880
The cafeteria's on the floor below!

22
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:39,880
That's not what's important now!

23
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,350
Maybe I can't stop it firing, but...

24
00:02:50,010 --> 00:02:52,810
She's so absurdly strong...

25
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:55,430
Sorry, ma'am.

26
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:59,400
I made a big hole in the roof.

27
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:03,690
W-Well, that's not so bad...

28
00:03:04,070 --> 00:03:06,130
It's going to come back down, though.

29
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:10,660
We need Artifacts to 
defeat a magicite beast.

30
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:14,050
It's going to land in the schoolyard!

31
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:17,000
When it does, I'll finish it off.

32
00:03:18,670 --> 00:03:19,960
Wait!

33
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:24,130
Yua, it's dangerous there!

34
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:27,590
Above you! Above you!

35
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,600
Run away!

36
00:03:36,890 --> 00:03:37,810
Chop!

37
00:03:45,310 --> 00:03:47,730
Yua's amazing...

38
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,390
<i>I may have already damaged it with my kick,</i>

39
00:03:50,390 --> 00:03:53,190
<i>but she still managed to chop it in half 
with a wave of her hand.</i>

40
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,210
<i>She's as strong as I thought!</i>

41
00:03:56,300 --> 00:04:00,170
Will we not see any more 
magicite beasts for a while?

42
00:04:00,470 --> 00:04:04,490
Yes. We learned in the last battle

43
00:04:04,490 --> 00:04:08,700
that Ripple absorbs mana 
from Special-class Rune bearers

44
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:11,130
and uses it to summon magicite beasts.

45
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:14,880
And summoning that magicite beast 
drained the mana she'd built up.

46
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:20,420
We won't see another one until 
her mana builds up again, right?

47
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:23,220
You understand well.

48
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:25,440
Um, I have another question.

49
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:31,020
Why do all the summoned magicite beasts 
appear to be former demihumans?

50
00:04:31,290 --> 00:04:34,760
Probably because Ripple 
herself is a demihuman.

51
00:04:35,130 --> 00:04:39,670
Demihumans have what you 
might call a sixth sense.

52
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:42,220
It's said they could even use telepathy.

53
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:47,680
She's using that species-wide 
connection to summon them.

54
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:49,770
Is that why?

55
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:53,880
Which is why what they did 
could only be done to Ripple.

56
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:59,090
It's even possible they created a demihuman 
Hyral Menas specifically for this purpose.

57
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:02,780
I feel bad for Ripple,

58
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:04,830
having her friends used in such a way.

59
00:05:05,230 --> 00:05:09,130
A lot of Highlanders don't see people 
on the surface as their equals,

60
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:11,330
which leads to this way of thinking.

61
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:13,780
It's embarrassing.

62
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,360
Now, now, everyone.

63
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,780
It's all in how you think about it!

64
00:05:17,170 --> 00:05:20,790
My comrades have been stuck 
as magicite beasts all this time,

65
00:05:20,790 --> 00:05:22,750
so this way, we can finally let them rest.

66
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:25,490
As long as nobody around us gets hurt.

67
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:30,850
Of course! We'll make sure they don't!

68
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:35,110
Thanks, everyone.

69
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:36,140
Excuse me.

70
00:05:36,710 --> 00:05:38,090
Come in!

71
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,970
Brother Raf!

72
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:42,870
Eris!

73
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:44,880
I've been worried about you.

74
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,470
Tell me how you're doing later.

75
00:05:46,470 --> 00:05:48,080
Right now, we have urgent news.

76
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:51,280
Is something wrong, you two?

77
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:54,740
The neighboring country of Venefic 
has violated our borders.

78
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:59,930
Prince Wein is asking for Sir Theodore 
to return to the castle immediately.

79
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:04,920
Two Weeks Later

80
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:04,920
What a great bath!

81
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:09,960
I'm glad nothing happened 
when we were on duty today!

82
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:12,390
I think one person here 
would disagree with you.

83
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:16,530
We haven't seen a single 
magicite beast since then!

84
00:06:16,530 --> 00:06:18,210
That's a good thing!

85
00:06:18,210 --> 00:06:20,670
You're right, but...

86
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:24,840
Don't you think we need a place where 
we can show off the results of our training?

87
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,430
I don't think that, no.

88
00:06:26,430 --> 00:06:29,980
It's better for Ripple that nothing happens.

89
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:32,410
I get that, but...

90
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:36,370
Liselotte, have you heard 
what's going on near the border?

91
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:41,320
There's a standoff going on right now, 
I heard. But nothing beyond that...

92
00:06:41,320 --> 00:06:45,670
So the Prismer's still not 
doing anything either, huh?

93
00:06:47,330 --> 00:06:51,510
That's the kind of sigh you make 
when the one you like won't notice you.

94
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:56,720
Well, Chris does say her 
ideal type is a Prismer.

95
00:06:56,720 --> 00:07:02,200
It always feels like Chris is a totally 
different person on the inside and outside.

96
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,160
Yes.

97
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:06,140
Her body is Boobs, but her brain is Muscles.

98
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:07,860
Yua!

99
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:10,760
<i>I couldn't even sense her approach.</i>

100
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:12,030
<i>Impressive!</i>

101
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:13,050
<i>Wait...</i>

102
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:15,090
<i>If there aren't any magicite beasts...</i>

103
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:16,840
Yua!

104
00:07:17,330 --> 00:07:21,890
The way you chopped that magicite 
beast in half was amazing!

105
00:07:21,890 --> 00:07:24,910
I'd love it if you could 
show me how it was done!

106
00:07:24,910 --> 00:07:26,870
In a battle, preferably!

107
00:07:26,870 --> 00:07:27,610
I refuse.

108
00:07:27,610 --> 00:07:29,290
Why?

109
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:31,510
I don't like physical exercise.

110
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:33,900
Well, it's hard for me to respond to that...

111
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:36,670
What can I do to make you tell me?

112
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,800
Yua?

113
00:07:40,190 --> 00:07:42,730
There's something I want you 
to teach me, too.

114
00:07:42,730 --> 00:07:45,950
If you do, I'll fight you, 
or do anything else you want.

115
00:07:45,950 --> 00:07:47,400
Really?

116
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:48,660
What is it?

117
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:51,270
I'll teach you anything you want to know!

118
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:54,160
How can I get my boobs that big, too?

119
00:07:55,370 --> 00:07:59,330
Um, well... mine kinda just grew this way.

120
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:01,360
That doesn't tell me anything.

121
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,810
I want to have huge boobs 
so everyone likes me!

122
00:08:04,170 --> 00:08:07,290
I want to show off my cleavage 
to the entire world, like you do, Boobs!

123
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,990
I don't do that!

124
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:14,820
If you can teach me a way 
to make my breasts bigger,

125
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:16,770
I'll fight you as much as you want!

126
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,730
Leone!

127
00:08:18,730 --> 00:08:21,120
I-I don't know either!

128
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:24,180
Plus, they're heavy, they make your 
shoulders stiff, and people stare!

129
00:08:24,180 --> 00:08:25,480
There's nothing good about them.

130
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:28,300
You're lucky you get 
to worry about that stuff!

131
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:30,730
You don't know how us flat girls live!

132
00:08:31,330 --> 00:08:34,910
So Rafinha's taking Yua's side?

133
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:39,010
You don't have to worry, 
because you've got proper boobs.

134
00:08:39,010 --> 00:08:41,050
And they're not big enough 
to strain your shoulders.

135
00:08:41,050 --> 00:08:43,340
In a way, they're the best size.

136
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:45,700
I don't know about that...

137
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:49,910
And you don't have to deal with 
Lyn playing around in there.

138
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:53,230
I think Liselotte ought to 
experience that at least once.

139
00:08:55,310 --> 00:08:57,000
Go, Lyn!

140
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:03,490
N-No! It tickles!

141
00:09:03,490 --> 00:09:04,770
Hey!

142
00:09:04,770 --> 00:09:08,370
Somebody help me!

143
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:11,830
Liselotte was really mad...

144
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:15,250
She was intense. I was scared.

145
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,120
Rafinha!

146
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:20,150
I have something to give to you!

147
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:24,380
Change into your uniform and come 
to the principal's office, would you?

148
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:29,810
Theodore says this is for you.

149
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:33,990
I this a new Artifact?

150
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:39,690
Yes. It has the same base as 
your current "Shiny Flow,"

151
00:09:39,690 --> 00:09:42,770
but it's an upgraded version 
with a second Gift as well.

152
00:09:42,770 --> 00:09:45,420
Wow! Thank you!

153
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:51,130
I'm surprised Theodore has any time to make 
Artifacts, with how busy he is right now,

154
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:53,140
but this is a great help!

155
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:54,420
Yes!

156
00:09:54,420 --> 00:10:01,620
Also, the second power that 
Artifact has is one of healing.

157
00:10:02,210 --> 00:10:05,570
I've never heard of an Artifact 
with that kind of power!

158
00:10:05,570 --> 00:10:10,030
It's quite rare and difficult to make.

159
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:13,480
That's why he wants you to have it, he says.

160
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,570
Theodore...

161
00:10:16,570 --> 00:10:22,480
He also asks that you take care 
of Ripple for him.

162
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:23,850
Of course!

163
00:10:23,850 --> 00:10:27,340
I'll protect Ripple and everyone else!

164
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:30,920
I'll have to start training right now 
so that I can use it properly!

165
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,450
Sure you do.

166
00:10:32,450 --> 00:10:37,330
Chris, you always make that face 
whenever Theodore is involved!

167
00:10:37,330 --> 00:10:39,580
I am not making a face.

168
00:10:44,150 --> 00:10:45,420
That's...

169
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:48,540
Hurry and put out the fire!

170
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:51,510
The magicite beast has been defeated. 
The flames need putting out, now!

171
00:10:52,070 --> 00:10:53,540
What's going on?

172
00:10:54,130 --> 00:10:55,470
Principal Miliera!

173
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:58,910
Ripple summoned more magicite beasts.

174
00:10:58,910 --> 00:11:02,680
We sealed them in a pocket space 
and fought them, but...

175
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:04,530
Silva!

176
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,360
Silva!

177
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:08,160
Silva?

178
00:11:11,890 --> 00:11:13,940
He's horribly wounded...

179
00:11:15,270 --> 00:11:16,220
I'm fine.

180
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:19,640
Forget about me, and get Ripple out of here.

181
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:22,240
I can't let her see me like this.

182
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:24,570
Make sure she's safe!

183
00:11:24,570 --> 00:11:25,250
Okay!

184
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:31,280
For someone as strong as you 
to be this badly injured...

185
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:33,650
It must have been a powerful 
magicite beast indeed.

186
00:11:34,150 --> 00:11:37,960
I'm so sorry... It was my failure.

187
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:40,920
No! It's not your fault!

188
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:42,430
It's their fault!

189
00:11:42,770 --> 00:11:43,990
"Their fault"?

190
00:11:45,430 --> 00:11:46,740
I'm sorry...

191
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:49,970
Rati... Pram?

192
00:11:49,970 --> 00:11:51,320
What happened?

193
00:11:52,190 --> 00:11:56,890
He protected me when a magicite 
beast was about to kill me...

194
00:11:56,890 --> 00:11:57,920
and he was badly hurt.

195
00:11:58,550 --> 00:12:03,600
N-No! Rati tried to protect <i>me</i>!

196
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,440
So it's my fault!

197
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,730
I'm so sorry!

198
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:08,640
"Sorry" won't cut it!

199
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,210
Thanks to you, Silva is...

200
00:12:11,210 --> 00:12:12,390
Stop.

201
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:17,450
My lack of care when activating the pocket 
space caused them to be caught up in it.

202
00:12:17,450 --> 00:12:18,870
The mistake was all mine.

203
00:12:19,170 --> 00:12:23,250
And as someone with power,

204
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:26,300
it's my job to protect 
the powerless Runeless.

205
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:28,630
Were you hurt?

206
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:31,250
No. Not even a scratch.

207
00:12:31,610 --> 00:12:33,040
I see.

208
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:34,690
Then...

209
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,980
Silva?

210
00:12:37,490 --> 00:12:39,690
Silva! Silva!

211
00:12:40,090 --> 00:12:42,340
Oh, no! We need to hurry and 
get him to the medical room!

212
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:43,660
Wait!

213
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,600
I'll try and help.

214
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,520
The healing Gift...

215
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,570
Please, go ahead!

216
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:51,940
Okay!

217
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:53,250
You'll be okay.

218
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:54,540
You can do it, Rani.

219
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,020
Does anything feel "wrong"?

220
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,190
Yes.

221
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:14,410
That's good. It means that your power is 
flowing to a different Gift than usual.

222
00:13:14,410 --> 00:13:16,100
Please continue.

223
00:13:16,780 --> 00:13:19,360
Focus on what lies just 
beyond your fingertips.

224
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,580
Okay...

225
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:23,480
<i>So this is the healing Gift...</i>

226
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:29,150
<i>The movements of the mana are so complex, 
I don't think I could easily recreate it...</i>

227
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:34,640
Now hold that light up to Silva.

228
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,780
Okay!

229
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:44,870
His wounds...

230
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,170
They're healing!

231
00:13:49,570 --> 00:13:53,260
<i>So the healing Gift places 
a heavy strain on its user?</i>

232
00:13:53,710 --> 00:13:54,620
<i>Then...</i>

233
00:13:57,510 --> 00:13:59,350
Rani. I'll help you.

234
00:13:59,710 --> 00:14:02,550
<i>I can't copy the mana the Gift uses.</i>

235
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:05,090
<i>But if I just create mana with 
a wavelength similar to Rani's...</i>

236
00:14:05,090 --> 00:14:06,370
Chris?

237
00:14:06,770 --> 00:14:08,140
Think you can do it?

238
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:11,020
Yeah! I can do a lot more now!

239
00:14:24,770 --> 00:14:26,790
He's okay now, isn't he?

240
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:29,130
Thank you both.

241
00:14:29,130 --> 00:14:31,650
Now, get him to the medical room.

242
00:14:31,650 --> 00:14:32,550
Okay!

243
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:36,380
Thank you for saving Silva.

244
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:40,430
No... Anyone would have done the same.

245
00:14:42,370 --> 00:14:45,140
Thanks, Chris! You were a huge help!

246
00:15:02,530 --> 00:15:05,190
Are the two of you okay?

247
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:06,270
We're fine...

248
00:15:06,570 --> 00:15:08,430
Really?

249
00:15:08,430 --> 00:15:09,980
That's...

250
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:12,430
The super-spicy meal!

251
00:15:12,770 --> 00:15:15,400
It's so spicy!

252
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,240
But it's good!

253
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:19,090
It sure wakes you up, huh?

254
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:23,560
Super-spicy food reminds me of home, though.

255
00:15:23,790 --> 00:15:25,780
Where did you say you were from?

256
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,470
Alucard, in the north.

257
00:15:29,210 --> 00:15:33,150
It's cold up there, so you eat 
spicy food to warm yourself up.

258
00:15:33,690 --> 00:15:36,570
So we're used to eating really spicy food.

259
00:15:36,570 --> 00:15:39,900
It reminds us of home!

260
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:42,120
You want some too, then?

261
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:45,070
I'd love some, but... there's so much...

262
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:48,050
I'll give you some of mine.

263
00:15:48,390 --> 00:15:51,080
Th-Thanks...

264
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:53,000
Give me some too, Inglis!

265
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,700
Sure thing!

266
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:55,720
No!

267
00:15:56,130 --> 00:15:57,550
Why?

268
00:15:57,550 --> 00:15:59,930
No indirect kisses!

269
00:15:59,930 --> 00:16:02,450
Sure, sure. Got it.

270
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:06,140
You're just doing what Pram 
tells you today, huh?

271
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:10,100
Well, I did kinda screw up yesterday.

272
00:16:10,100 --> 00:16:12,440
I owe you guys a big thank-you, too.

273
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:15,710
No, it's not your fault!

274
00:16:15,710 --> 00:16:18,540
You just tried to help me...

275
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:21,910
But I had to be saved 
by somebody else instead!

276
00:16:22,490 --> 00:16:25,610
I need to apologize to Silva.

277
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:30,090
I don't think he was mad, though.

278
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:32,870
Yeah. He was sticking up for you.

279
00:16:32,870 --> 00:16:39,560
He was kind of a jerk when we first met, 
so I thought he just hated squires.

280
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,600
Oh, I get it!

281
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:44,770
He must be one of those guys 
who likes young boys!

282
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:47,730
That's why he was so kind to Rati!

283
00:16:47,730 --> 00:16:48,730
Well?

284
00:16:48,730 --> 00:16:51,050
That can't be right!

285
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:54,700
Yeah, I really can't handle any more rivals!

286
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:58,000
So why was he so harsh on me?

287
00:16:58,830 --> 00:17:03,360
Cause you're a girl, Chris! Obviously!

288
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:06,020
He just likes young boys...

289
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:09,090
I'd prefer you didn't jump to 
conclusions about people like that.

290
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:11,390
Silva?

291
00:17:11,390 --> 00:17:13,480
Are you feeling better?

292
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:16,040
Yes. The scars are almost all gone, too.

293
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:17,750
That Gift of yours is incredible.

294
00:17:17,750 --> 00:17:21,230
Um, I'm so sorry about yesterday.

295
00:17:21,230 --> 00:17:23,060
We're really sorry.

296
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:27,520
Don't worry about it. It was 
my mistake to begin with.

297
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:32,930
And in the end, you were 
the ones who saved me.

298
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:35,770
Let me apologize for my rudeness 
and thank you properly.

299
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:37,410
Thank you.

300
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:43,940
Not at all... I'm sorry we were such brats!

301
00:17:44,370 --> 00:17:45,930
I'm sorry!

302
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:50,800
Now we've all apologized, 
so we're even, right?

303
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:56,840
Yes.

304
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,700
Let's say that we are.

305
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:05,590
Okay, your turn's over, Rani.

306
00:18:05,590 --> 00:18:07,100
My turn now.

307
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:11,810
We ate a whole lot!

308
00:18:11,810 --> 00:18:13,700
Let's do our best to defend 
Ripple this afternoon!

309
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:17,370
Sure, but since Silva and his group 
defeated the magicite beast,

310
00:18:17,370 --> 00:18:20,880
we won't see another for a while.

311
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:24,760
Chris...

312
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,430
They can't do this!

313
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:29,280
Come in!

314
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,340
Excuse us.

315
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:35,020
It's time for our shift to begin.

316
00:18:35,810 --> 00:18:37,630
Thanks for coming.

317
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:41,340
Um. It sounds like something 
had upset you...

318
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:44,640
Oh, I'm sorry. I couldn't help myself.

319
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:47,580
Actually, the Royal Guard sent a demand to us

320
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:51,480
that we turn Ripple over 
to them for protection.

321
00:18:52,790 --> 00:18:54,940
Why now, after everything?

322
00:18:54,940 --> 00:19:01,850
They say they're sending Ripple back to the 
Highland and getting a new Hyral Menas.

323
00:19:02,590 --> 00:19:08,680
But... You can't replace her just 
because she's a little sick...

324
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:10,760
That's treating her like 
an object, not a person!

325
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:15,210
We will continue to keep 
her safe at the academy.

326
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,510
Right?

327
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:22,250
But, Miliera, if you get into 
a fight with the Royal Guard,

328
00:19:22,250 --> 00:19:24,210
won't that cause problems for everyone?

329
00:19:24,210 --> 00:19:26,940
Not in the least.

330
00:19:26,940 --> 00:19:30,940
Protecting you is what we all want to do.

331
00:19:31,230 --> 00:19:33,900
She's right!

332
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:36,140
Leave it to us!

333
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:38,700
Guys...

334
00:19:43,150 --> 00:19:46,400
Prism Flow? Now of all times?

335
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:51,510
The magicite beasts don't care 
what we've got going on in our lives.

336
00:19:51,510 --> 00:19:56,120
What's the principal 
going to do about Ripple?

337
00:19:56,540 --> 00:20:01,800
She's sending a formal message to 
Prince Wein, as a means of buying time.

338
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:06,680
That's why Rati and Pram 
ran off in the Flying Gears.

339
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:10,430
The prince is away right now.

340
00:20:10,430 --> 00:20:12,410
It's bad timing.

341
00:20:12,410 --> 00:20:17,350
They were excited to make up 
for their failure before, though.

342
00:20:18,090 --> 00:20:19,320
What's wrong?

343
00:20:20,230 --> 00:20:22,780
Bad timing...

344
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:27,170
Oh, well, there's nothing 
we can do about the rain.

345
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:33,950
No, I mean the way the Royal Guard is 
doing this when Prince Wein isn't around.

346
00:20:33,950 --> 00:20:37,700
If somebody is pulling strings 
behind the scenes...

347
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:42,090
Leone!

348
00:20:42,090 --> 00:20:43,330
On it!

349
00:20:52,870 --> 00:20:54,470
A lightning beast...

350
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:59,820
That's the power of my brother's Artifact!

351
00:21:32,430 --> 00:21:34,290
Brother Leon!

352
00:21:34,290 --> 00:21:37,440
Hey. It's been a long time, Leone.

353
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:39,670
Wait!

354
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:44,150
Somebody else is here.

355
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,830
Who's there?!

356
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:04,830
It can't be...

357
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:10,470
The Bloodchain Brigade!

358
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,060
Silva is
 a rival,
 too?

359
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,060
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

360
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,060
That's
imposs-
ible!

361
00:23:46,070 --> 00:23:51,060
Comic by Kuromura Moto

